<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Speed in knots and kilometres per hour</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>A cargo ship sails due [[if test="north"]]north[[else]]south[[/if]] along a meridian from port \(P\) (latitude \([[if test="is(ix=1)"]]2^\circ\,10'\,\mathrm{S}[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=2)"]]1^\circ\,40'\,\mathrm{N}[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=3)"]]8^\circ\,05'\,\mathrm{S}[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=4)"]]0^\circ\,50'\,\mathrm{S}[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=5)"]]4^\circ\,15'\,\mathrm{S}[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=6)"]]3^\circ\,30'\,\mathrm{N}[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=7)"]]5^\circ\,00'\,\mathrm{S}[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=8)"]]6^\circ\,10'\,\mathrm{S}[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=9)"]]2^\circ\,20'\,\mathrm{N}[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=10)"]]7^\circ\,40'\,\mathrm{S}[[/if]]\)) to port \(Q\) (latitude \([[if test="is(ix=1)"]]4^\circ\,25'\,\mathrm{S}[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=2)"]]3^\circ\,05'\,\mathrm{S}[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=3)"]]5^\circ\,20'\,\mathrm{S}[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=4)"]]3^\circ\,35'\,\mathrm{N}[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=5)"]]7^\circ\,55'\,\mathrm{S}[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=6)"]]6^\circ\,45'\,\mathrm{N}[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=7)"]]0^\circ\,35'\,\mathrm{N}[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=8)"]]9^\circ\,00'\,\mathrm{S}[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=9)"]]1^\circ\,55'\,\mathrm{S}[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=10)"]]4^\circ\,50'\,\mathrm{S}[[/if]]\)). It leaves at \([[if test="is(floor(mod(dep,1440)/60)<10)"]]0[[/if]]{@floor(mod(dep,1440)/60)@}:[[if test="is(mod(mod(dep,1440),60)<10)"]]0[[/if]]{@mod(mod(dep,1440),60)@}\) and arrives at \([[if test="is(floor(mod(arr,1440)/60)<10)"]]0[[/if]]{@floor(mod(arr,1440)/60)@}:[[if test="is(mod(mod(arr,1440),60)<10)"]]0[[/if]]{@mod(mod(arr,1440),60)@}\)[[if test="nxt"]] the next day[[/if]].</p><p>(a) Find the distance it sails, in nautical miles.</p><p>[[input:ans1]] nm [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>(b) Find its average speed in knots, correct to 1 decimal place.</p><p>[[input:ans2]] knots [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p><p>(c) Find its average speed in km/h, correct to the nearest km/h. Take \(1\) knot \(= 1.853\) km/h.</p><p>[[input:ans3]] km/h [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) [[if test="same"]]Both ports are on the same side of the equator, so subtract the latitudes.[[else]]The ports are on opposite sides of the equator, so add the latitudes.[[/if]] The difference is \({@floor((nm)/60)@}^\circ\,[[if test="is(mod(nm,60)<10)"]]0[[/if]]{@mod(nm,60)@}' = {@nm@}'\), and along a meridian \(1'\) is \(1\) nm, so the ship sails \({@nm@}\) nm.</p><p>(b) The journey lasts \({@dh@}\) h \({@dm@}\) min \(= {@dh@} + \tfrac{ {@dm@} }{60} = {@dispdp(float(dur/60),2)@}\) h. A knot is one nautical mile per hour, so the speed is \({@nm@} \div {@dispdp(float(dur/60),2)@} = {@dispdp(float(kn),3)@} \approx {@dispdp(float(floor(10*kn+1/2)/10),1)@}\) knots.</p><p>(c) \({@dispdp(float(kn),3)@} \times 1.853 = {@dispdp(float(kmh),2)@} \approx {@floor(kmh+1/2)@}\) km/h.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
